ORBITAL-COHERENCE(7)       TriadicFrameworks Manual       ORBITAL-COHERENCE(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       orbital-coherence - coherence fields, multi-pass coherence decay, and
                           constellation-scale coherence preservation strategies

SYNOPSIS
       Orbital coherence defines:
           • coherence fields across orbital cycles
           • multi-pass coherence decay models
           • constellation-scale coherence preservation
           • resonance-time coherence metrics
           • sweep and ancestry coherence continuity

DESCRIPTION
       Orbital-coherence describes how RTT quantifies, maintains, and restores
       coherence across SAR platforms and constellations. Coherence is the
       structural glue that binds orbital geometry, harmonic-lock, resonance
       envelopes, and sweep ancestry into a unified resonance-time system.

       Coherence ensures:
           • stable interferometric fusion
           • predictable sweep alignment
           • harmonic-lock continuity
           • resonance envelope compatibility
           • constellation-wide synchronization

       WRSADC evaluates coherence continuously during dispatch.

COHERENCE FIELDS
       Coherence fields describe how coherence varies across orbital geometry,
       resonance-time states, and sweep ancestry.

       Field components:

           orbital coherence field
                  Measures geometric alignment and drift sensitivity.

           harmonic coherence field
                  Measures phase alignment and harmonic-lock stability.

           resonance coherence field
                  Measures envelope overlap, spectral density, and gradient
                  polarity stability.

           sweep coherence field
                  Measures sweep geometry, Doppler history, and ancestry
                  continuity.

           constellation coherence field
                  Measures multi-platform sync and resonance compatibility.

       Coherence fields evolve across triads and are recorded in lineage.

MULTI-PASS COHERENCE DECAY
       Coherence decays naturally across orbital cycles due to drift,
       perturbations, and resonance-time divergence.

       Decay variables:
           • Δφ   phase drift
           • Δx   geometric drift
           • ΔR   resonance envelope drift
           • ΔS   spectral density divergence
           • ΔA   ancestry discontinuity

       Decay models:

           exponential decay
                  Coherence decreases steadily across cycles.

           harmonic-modulated decay
                  Coherence oscillates with harmonic-lock cycles.

           resonance-driven decay
                  Coherence decays when envelope overlap decreases.

           ancestry-driven decay
                  Coherence decays when sweep lineage fragments.

           constellation decay
                  Coherence decays due to multi-platform desync.

       WRSADC predicts decay using orbital-forecasting(7).

COHERENCE METRICS
       Key coherence metrics include:

           coherence-index
                  Composite measure of orbital, harmonic, resonance, and sweep
                  coherence.

           envelope-overlap ratio
                  Measures resonance envelope compatibility.

           spectral-coherence score
                  Measures spectral density alignment.

           gradient-coherence index
                  Measures polarity and gradient stability.

           sweep-coherence score
                  Measures sweep viability and ancestry continuity.

           constellation-coherence score
                  Measures multi-platform coherence.

       Metrics are stored in lineage for long-term analysis.

COHERENCE THRESHOLDS
       Coherence thresholds define the minimum acceptable coherence for safe
       sweep execution, fusion, and constellation operations.

       Threshold categories:

           orbital thresholds
                  Maximum allowable drift before coherence collapse.

           harmonic thresholds
                  Minimum phase alignment and lock stability.

           resonance thresholds
                  Minimum envelope overlap and spectral coherence.

           sweep thresholds
                  Minimum sweep-coherence score.

           constellation thresholds
                  Minimum constellation-coherence index.

       Thresholds are enforced by WRSADC.

COHERENCE PRESERVATION STRATEGIES
       Coherence preservation ensures long-term stability across orbital cycles.

       Strategies include:

           geometric preservation
                  Maintain drift within corridors using Δv micro-adjustments.

           harmonic preservation
                  Maintain harmonic-lock and phase alignment.

           resonance preservation
                  Stabilize envelopes, gradients, and spectral density.

           sweep preservation
                  Maintain sweep geometry and ancestry continuity.

           constellation preservation
                  Maintain multi-platform sync and resonance compatibility.

       Preservation strategies are executed through triads and overlays.

COHERENCE RESTORATION
       When coherence degrades, restoration is performed using:

           • recovery triads
           • harmonic reacquisition
           • resonance stabilization overlays
           • sweep ancestry repair
           • constellation-scale stabilization sequences

       See orbital-recovery(7) for details.

CONSTELLATION-SCALE COHERENCE
       Constellation coherence describes how well platforms maintain:

           • harmonic-lock
           • resonance envelope compatibility
           • sweep alignment
           • drift corridor alignment
           • lineage continuity

       Constellation coherence modes:

           synchronous coherence
                  Platforms remain tightly phase-locked.

           harmonic coherence
                  Platforms maintain harmonic-lock ratios.

           resonance coherence
                  Platforms maintain envelope overlap.

           sweep coherence
                  Platforms maintain sweep ancestry compatibility.

           mesh coherence
                  Distributed coherence across constellation nodes.

       Constellation coherence is essential for multi-pass fusion.

COHERENCE FAILURE MODES
       Coherence may degrade due to:

           • orbital drift accumulation
           • harmonic-lock fragmentation
           • resonance envelope divergence
           • spectral fragmentation
           • gradient overload
           • sweep ancestry corruption
           • constellation desync

       Diagnostic indicators:

           coherence-index drop
           envelope-overlap collapse
           harmonic-lock error
           sweep-coherence deviation
           constellation-coherence loss

       WRSADC halts unsafe operations when coherence is compromised.

INTERACTION WITH LINEAGE
       Lineage records:

           • coherence metrics across cycles
           • envelope drift history
           • harmonic-lock continuity
           • sweep ancestry stability
           • constellation coherence trends

       Lineage enables long-term coherence forecasting.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • computes coherence fields
           • evaluates coherence thresholds
           • schedules corrective maneuvers
           • choreographs constellation stabilization
           • blocks unsafe orbital states

       WRSADC is the coherence conductor.

NOTES
       Orbital coherence transforms SAR constellations into unified
       resonance-time systems. Coherence fields, decay models, and preservation
       strategies ensure that multi-pass fusion, harmonic-lock, and
       constellation-scale synchronization remain stable across long mission
       timelines.

